{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>And he shall besiege you in all your gates.</b> That is, in every place. And it may be explained that the reason he mentioned 'your gates' four times in the parashah: the first is general, the second the gates of the cities, the third the gates of private houses, and the fourth from the root of שעור (measure/reckoning) — that is, that the enemy will distress him in everything he contemplates, and trouble and harm will befall him and terror overtake him in everything he reckons to do. And behold, this is the reverse of the successful man, who prospers wherever he turns and succeeds in whatever he thinks, and all his words and thoughts turn out aright — as stated concerning the wicked man (Psalms 10): ״יחילו דרכיו בכל עת״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:46.971185670Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}